		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "c81f23ec-80a2-4043-acd4-07184e8fbff5")
		(at 55.5 34.5)
		(descr "TCXO, Connor-Winfield CWX113-100.0M (per datasheets/extracted/ev-radar-mmic2.md BOM: Y1, 100MHz reference for ADF4159/ADF5901 REFIN). Package/land pattern per datasheets/CWX113_SM118.pdf (Connor-Winfield Bulletin Sm118 Rev.13, 'Xxxx-Series' 5.0x7.0mm LVCMOS Clock Oscillator family; X113 = 0-70C, +/-25ppm, 3.3Vdc member of this family, per support-parts.md's confirmed reasoning that Sm118 is the correct primary source for CWX113 -- no separate 'CWX113'-titled PDF exists, and no exposed pad on this package). Body: D=5.0mm nom (4.85-5.15) x E=7.0mm nom (6.86-7.16), p.2 Package Outline table. 4-pad SMD-no-lead, 2x2 corner-pad layout per p.2 'Suggested Pad Layout': pad size 1.40mm(X) x 1.64mm(Y) (derived from datasheet's explicit 4.2mm total keepout width, 5.08mm total pad-layout height, 1.8mm inter-pad vertical gap, and lead width b=1.40mm from the Package Outline table), pad centers at +/-1.40mm(X)/+/-1.72mm(Y). Supersedes the prior TCXO_CWX823_5.0X7.0MM.kicad_mod footprint, which was authored from the eval-schematic's CWX823 footprint reference before the CWX113-specific Sm118 PDF was available on disk; reconciled to CWX113 per ev-radar-mmic2.md's BOM (CWX113-100.0M is the fitted part) and support-parts.md's symbol-side verification. Renamed from TCXO_CWX823_5.0X7.0MM to TCXO_CWX113_SMD4 to match the symbol's Footprint property.")
